  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have two systems with VRChat. One is with GTX1060 and other is older AMD HD7870 videocard.\n\nThere are no problems with GTX1060. I can walk very near avatar and i can put my hand on the head and pet the avatar.\nThat is good. \n\nNow i move to other PC with older HD7870. Yeah, that is pretty old one but it can hold pretty much. I know the drivers are not very latest.\nBecause there is strange problem with VRChat when i walk to very near avatar. It suddenly vanished. I cannot touch or pet or hug it. Booo....\n\nI think it might driver issue, but it's program like other programs, and other games have no strange clipping problems with HD7870.\n\nI need more confirm to check if it's driver related problem, or it's wrong setting in VRChat with AMD driver.\n\nI want ask to other AMD videocard users if they have same problems as me. The avatar will just vanish (or hide) when you want walk very near and touch it.\n\nThank you.",
